WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.715
Microsoft's path is a phased
move toward cloud-first,

2
00:00:03.715 --> 00:00:08.062
not an all-at-once decommission,
and AD itself isn't deprecated.

3
00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:11.312
What changes is where the
DNS records come from.

4
00:00:11.312 --> 00:00:15.525
Entra ID publishes no zones
and no locator records.

5
00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:19.499
Entra-joined devices use tokens;
hybrid-joined devices still

6
00:00:19.499 --> 00:00:23.550
look for a domain controller,
and Kerberos survives in pockets.

7
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.694
Here's the failure to recognize:
resolve a name to the wrong host,

8
00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.875
and a valid ticket for computer A gets
presented to computer B, which rejects it.

9
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:36.950
It looks like an identity
problem, but the cause is DNS.

10
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.315
So before any domain controller goes,

11
00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:43.739
keep locator records resolvable
until every consumer is token-based,

12
00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:48.910
test and prune the forwarders, and move
each remaining zone type by its own method.
